    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A confederation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#germanic-peoples">Germanic peoples</a> on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rhine">Rhine</a>, formed in the 3rd century from older groups such as the Chamavi and Bructeri.</li><li>Franks raided Roman Gaul but also served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rome">Rome</a>, reaching the highest commands under generals such as Arbogast and Bauto.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#childeric-i">Childeric I</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#clovis-i">Clovis I</a> turned the confederation into the Frankish kingdom from which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#germany">Germany</a> grew.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#childeric-i">Childeric I</a>’s grave at Tournai, found in 1653, held some 300 gold bees or cicadas; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#napoleon">Napoleon</a> adopted the bee as an imperial emblem partly in their memory.</p></aside>
    </section>

